{
  "id": "m64l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Diagonal y aplanar",
    "en": "Diagonal and flatten"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Recorridos útiles"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "La **diagonal principal** son los elementos `m[i][i]`. **Aplanar** una matriz es convertirla en una sola lista, recorriendo fila a fila con una comprensión doble."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "m = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]",
          "print([m[i][i] for i in range(len(m))])",
          "print([x for fila in m for x in fila])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[1, 4]",
          "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "La comprensión doble `[x for fila in m for x in fila]` se lee como dos bucles anidados."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Useful traversals"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "The **main diagonal** are the elements `m[i][i]`. **Flattening** a matrix turns it into a single list, going row by row with a double comprehension."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "m = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]",
          "print([m[i][i] for i in range(len(m))])",
          "print([x for fila in m for x in fila])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[1, 4]",
          "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "The double comprehension `[x for fila in m for x in fila]` reads as two nested loops."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m64l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `diagonal(m)` que devuelva la diagonal principal de una matriz cuadrada.",
        "en": "Define `diagonal(m)` returning the main diagonal of a square matrix."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def diagonal(m):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def diagonal(m):",
        "    return [m[i][i] for i in range(len(m))]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "[m[i][i] for i in range(len(m))]."
        ],
        "en": [
          "[m[i][i] for i in range(len(m))]."
        ]
